{
  "total": 120,
  "totalPage": 3,
  "page": 3,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0ceff",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3351,
      "bookHadithIndex": 101,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Atiyyah bin ‘Amir Al-Juhani said:“I heard Salman, when he was forced to eat food, say: ‘It is sufficient for me that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: The people who most eat their fill in this world will be the most hungry on the Day of Resurrection.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3351-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3351-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3351-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3351-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf00",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3352,
      "bookHadithIndex": 102,
      "text": "It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“It is extravagance to eat everything you want.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3352-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3352-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3352-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3352-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf01",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3353,
      "bookHadithIndex": 103,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Aishah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the house and saw a piece of bread that had been thrown (on the floor). He picked it up, wiped it and ate it, and said: ‘O ‘Aishah, show honor to the precious (i.e., food), for is the blessing of food departs from people, it never comes back.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3353-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3353-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3353-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3353-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf02",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3354,
      "bookHadithIndex": 104,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: ‘Allahumma inni a’udhu bika minal-ju’, fa innahu bi’sad- daji’, wa a’udhu bika minal-khiyanah, fa innaha bi’satil-bitanah (O Allah, I seek refuge with You from hunger, for it is a bad companion, and I seek refuge with You from treachery, for it is a bad thing to hide in one’s heart).’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3354-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3354-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3354-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf03",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3355,
      "bookHadithIndex": 105,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir bin ‘Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Do not leave dinner, even if it is only a handful of dates, because abandoning it makes one weak.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3355-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3355-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3355-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sanad Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3355-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf04",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3356,
      "bookHadithIndex": 106,
      "text": "(It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah 9saw) said:“Goodness comes more quickly to a house where there are frequent guests than a knife to camel’s hump.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3356-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3356-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3356-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3356-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf05",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3357,
      "bookHadithIndex": 107,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn ‘Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Goodness comes more quickly to a house where food is eaten than a knife to a camel’s hump.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3357-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3357-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3357-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3357-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf06",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3358,
      "bookHadithIndex": 108,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“It is the Sunnah for a man to go out with his guest to the door of the house.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3358-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3358-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3358-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3358-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf07",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3359,
      "bookHadithIndex": 109,
      "text": "It was narrated that ‘Ali said:“I made some food and called the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) (to come and eat). He came and saw some images in the house, so he went back.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3359-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3359-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3359-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3359-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf08",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3360,
      "bookHadithIndex": 110,
      "text": "Safinah, Abu ‘Abdur-Rahman, narrated that a man visited ‘Ali bin Abu Talib and he made some food for him.* Fatimah said:“Why don’t we invite the Prophet (ﷺ) to eat with us?” So they invited him and he came. He put his hand on the doorpost of the house and saw a thin curtain in the corner of the house, so he went back. Fatimah said to ‘Ali: “Go and catch up with him, and ask him: ‘What made you go back, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “I do not enter a well-decorated house.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3360-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3360-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3360-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3360-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf09",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3361,
      "bookHadithIndex": 111,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said that ‘Umar entered upon him when he was eating, and he made room for him in the middle of the gathering. He said:Bismillah, then he took a morsel and ate it, then a second. Then he said: “I notice some fat in the food but it is not the fat of the meat.” ‘Abdullah said: “O Commander of the Believers! I went out to the marketplace looking for some fatty meat (bones with plenty of meat on them) to buy, but it was expensive, so I bought some lean meat (bones with not much meat on them) for a Dirham, and added a Dirham’s worth of ghee. I wanted my family to go through it bone by bone.” ‘Umar said: “The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never had these two things together; he would eat one and give the other in charity.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3361-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3361-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3361-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3361-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf0a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3362,
      "bookHadithIndex": 112,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Dharr that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“When you make broth, add more water and give some to your neighbor.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3362-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3362-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3362-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3362-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf0b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3363,
      "bookHadithIndex": 113,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ma’dan bin Abu Talhah Al-Ya’muri that ‘Umar bin Khattab stood up one Friday delivering a sermon. He praised and glorified Allah, then he said:“O people, you eat two plants which I do not regard as anything but offensive: This garlic and these onions. At the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), I would see a man, if the smell (of these vegetables) was found on him, being taken by the hand and led out to Baqi’ (graveyard). Whoever must eat them, let him cook them to death.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3363-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3363-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3363-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3363-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf0c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3364,
      "bookHadithIndex": 114,
      "text": "It was narrated that Umm Ayyub said:“I made some food for the Prophet (ﷺ) in which there were some vegetables. He did not eat it, and he said: ‘I do not like to annoy my companion.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3364-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3364-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3364-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3364-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf0d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3365,
      "bookHadithIndex": 115,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir that a group of people came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he noticed the smell of leeks coming from them. He said:“Did I not forbid you to eat these vegetables? For the angels are offended by that which offends people.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3365-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3365-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3365-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf0e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3366,
      "bookHadithIndex": 116,
      "text": "‘Uqbah bin ‘Amir Al-Juhani said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to his Companions: ‘Do not eat onions,’ then he said in a low voice: ‘Raw.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3366-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3366-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3366-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3366-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf0f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3367,
      "bookHadithIndex": 117,
      "text": "It was narrated that Salman Al-Farisi said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about ghee, cheese and wild donkeys. He said: ‘What is lawful is that which Allah has permitted, in His Book and what is unlawful is that which Allah has forbidden in His Book. What He remained silent about is what is pardoned.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3367-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3367-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3367-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c8bfdd1a4c9c86f0cf10",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 29,
      "hadithIndex": 3368,
      "bookHadithIndex": 118,
      "text": "It was narrated that Nu’man bin Bashir said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) was given a gift of some grapes from Ta’if. He called me and said: ‘Take this bunch of grapes and give it to your mother.’ But I ate it before I gave it to her. A few night later he said to me: ‘What happened to the bunch of grapes? Did you give it to your mother?’ I said: ‘No, So he called me treacherous.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3368-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-29-3368-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
